## Plotlines OSM/basemap mirror — issue #256 (Phase 1.2, epic #264).
## Serves /srv/plotlines-mirror (see build_tree.sh and README.md in this
## directory for the §6.3 tree layout) as plain static files.
##
## Three details that are not stylistic (docs/Plotlines_OSM_Acquisition_Review.md §6.4):
##  - The `http://` scheme prefix is required. Without it Caddy attempts
##    automatic HTTPS via ACME for a domain it cannot validate, and fails to
##    start.
##  - No `encode`. `.pmtiles` and `.osm.pbf` are already compressed, and
##    on-the-fly compression breaks byte-range semantics — exactly what
##    core/plotlines_core/tiles/extract.py:http_range_source needs.
##  - This must never be served with `python -m http.server`;
##    SimpleHTTPRequestHandler ignores Range and returns the whole file with
##    a 200, silently defeating every byte-range read.
##
## {$MIRROR_ROOT:...} keeps the production default (/srv/plotlines-mirror)
## while letting a local run point at a scratch tree without editing this
## file — the same "swap is a hostname/root change, nothing else" discipline
## §6.0 (Q6) asks of the tree itself.
##
## Issue #262 (Q1-C, §6.7): the one dynamic endpoint the mirror grows — bbox
## in, clipped .osm.pbf out — proxied to the mirror-clip container (see
## docker-compose.yml) so the client only ever needs this one hostname.
## `reverse_proxy`'s own path matcher terminates the request before
## `file_server` below ever sees a /clip request; everything else here stays
## plain static files, per §6.7's "everything else stays dumb."
http://tiles.plotlines.app {
	root * {$MIRROR_ROOT:/srv/plotlines-mirror}

	reverse_proxy /clip* {$MIRROR_CLIP_UPSTREAM:mirror-clip:8095}

	file_server

	# Build-pinned paths are immutable.
	header /basemap/* Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
	header /osm/*     Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"

	log {
		output file {$MIRROR_LOG:/var/log/caddy/mirror.log}
	}
}
